                                            (n, k)-Complete Hidden Subset Sum Problem
                                                            Lixia Luo∗, Changheng Li †, Qiongxiu Li ‡



                                                                                 Abstract
                                                       The Hidden Subset Sum Problem (HSSP) is a significant NP-
                                                   complete problem in number theory and combinatorics, with applica-
                                                   tions in cryptography and AI privacy. For the (n, k)-complete HSSP,
                                                   where a target multiset must be recovered from its all k-subset sums,
                                                   existing algorithms face limitations due to high complexity or in-
                                                   tractability. This paper proposes two deterministic algorithms: a
                                                   brute-force approach, and a novel method
